        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_148fba4f2a7140ce96d48b97b3a335ff",
      "statement": "Before the round-zero assessment and before each expansion-round assessment, the Runtime runs a budget probe that reuses the builder's own selection code and reports delivered, truncated, and dropped items plus unused bytes. The gate's budget-floor verdict uses budget_bounded, which is size-dependent: at the 512-byte floor, any dropped or truncated item or delivered content that used all headroom is budget-bound; above the floor, budget-bound requires exhausted headroom together with a dropped or truncated item, so fitting pressure alone is not sufficient for every budget. The budget-floor check runs only after the no-content check.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/powercontext/builtin/runtime/application.py#L1684-L1699",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4d200972d1a89a5e8ab679d6fdef8eef88947009166db9854cbe65b8a9363eff:"
